e seed path s, executing muon p on sampleOracle P g with budget T*B (single oracle) returns j |-> W_j (the trajectory) for j : Fin (T+1), provided B >= 1. True: the template run makes exactly T*B calls (remaining budget reaches 0 only after the last), call k receives g(point, s k), batch_full applied T times gives stateAt T, whose output is the trajectory; also correct when T = 0. This is the DEXEC1 execution correspondence and the cost-conversion witness for T41/T43 (T*B template calls = T iterations of B stochastic gradients).","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.execute_muon","source":["src_0382383352b1eed8e1076769","src_317f831b789ebedab301645c"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/inventory/declarations/3/type_text"],"comparison":"Statement (registered sorry body, not used as evidence): iterationStep at counter x.1 reads only samples with index < (x.1+1)B: true (it uses s(x.1 B + j), j < B).","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.iterationStep_congr","source":["src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_a758b6d08c4ce84a4dbfc684"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/inventory/declarations/4/type_text"],"comparison":"Auxiliary definition (not a source claim): the machine state after t complete iterations = (iter t, count 0, point W_t, momentum M_{t-1}, empty batch, iterates i <= t -> W_i else W0). At t = 0 it coincides with muon's initial state (momentum 0, all iterates W0). Used only to state the batch invariants.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.stateAt","source":["src_dd12a540fc285c40dd87082e","src_a8b804f2afa9050968e7d456"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/inventory/declarations/5/type_text"],"comparison":"Equation lemma of stateAt; restates its body.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.stateAt.eq_1","source":["src_dd12a540fc285c40dd87082e"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/inventory/declarations/6/type_text"],"comparison":"Statement (registered sorry body, not used as evidence): The counter component of trajectory t is t: true by induction.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.trajectory_fst","source":["src_dd12a540fc285c40dd87082e"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/inventory/declarations/7/type_text"],"comparison":"Statement (registered sorry body, not used as evidence): If (W, xi) |-> g W xi is jointly measurable, s |-> (W_t, M_{t-1}) is measurable on N -> Omega (product sigma-algebra) for each t: true (finite composition of measurable maps, using measurability of orthogonalize from the accepted matrix unit and of coordinate projections).","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.trajectory_measurable","source":["src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/inventory/declarations/8/type_text"],"comparison":"Statement (registered sorry body, not used as evidence): W_t (and M_{t-1}) depend only on samples s_j with j < tB: true by induction with iterationStep_congr. This is the adaptedness ('W_t depends only on samples before tB') required by DEXEC1 for the martingale argument of Lemma A.3.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.trajectory_prefix","source":["src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/inventory/declarations/9/type_text"],"comparison":"Statement (registered sorry body, not used as evidence): trajectory (t+1) = iterationStep (trajectory t): true (Function.iterate_succ_apply').","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.trajectory_succ","source":["src_dd12a540fc285c40dd87082e","src_a8b804f2afa9050968e7d456"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/inventory/declarations/10/type_text"],"comparison":"Statement (registered sorry body, not used as evidence): Unfolded recursion: W_{t+1} = W_t - eta orthogonalize(M_t), M_t = G_t if t = 0 else beta M_{t-1} + (1-beta) G_t with G_t = batchGradient at W_t using batch t: true (iterationStep with counter t); this is Algorithm 1 lines 203-206 verbatim.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.trajectory_succ_eq","source":["src_a758b6d08c4ce84a4dbfc684","src_32f